The E. coli cloning vector pBR322 carries two antibiotic resistance genes, each with restriction sites inside it:
- the **ampicillin resistance gene** (\(\text{amp}^{\text{R}}\)) has recognition sites for **Pst I** and Pvu I;
- the **tetracycline resistance gene** (\(\text{tet}^{\text{R}}\)) has recognition sites for BamH I and Sal I;
- EcoR I, Hind III and Cla I cut the plasmid outside these two genes.

So of the four enzymes listed, only Pst I cuts within the ampicillin resistance gene, and a foreign DNA ligated at that site inactivates ampicillin resistance. So the answer is option (C) Pst I.
